# Business Logic Model — Unit: pr-review-agent

## Overview
The agent is a Python module executed by a GitHub Actions workflow on the CodeBuild runner. It reviews the PR diff using Amazon Bedrock and reports results back to GitHub.

## End-to-End Flow

```
GitHub Actions (PR to dev: opened / reopened / synchronize)
      |
      v
[1] Load context (repo, PR number, head SHA, base ref) from GitHub event
      |
      v
[2] Guard: base ref == dev ?  --no--> exit (BR-PRA-01)
      |
      yes
      v
[3] Fetch PR diff via GitHub API  -> list[DiffFile]
      |
      v
[4] Size guard: total_diff_bytes > MAX_DIFF_BYTES ?
      |                                 |
      | yes                             | no
      v                                 v
 [4a] SKIPPED_TOO_LARGE           [5] Build size-bounded ReviewInput
      post split-PR comment            |
      set non-blocking check           v
      (BR-PRA-07)                 [6] Build prompt (delimited, injection-safe — BR-PRA-12)
      exit                             |
                                       v
                                  [7] Call Amazon Bedrock (Claude)
                                       |
                                 error | ok
                                       |
                             +---------+----------+
                             | error              | ok
                             v                    v
                       [7a] ERROR verdict   [8] Parse model JSON -> list[Finding]
                            fail-closed           |   (parse error -> ERROR, BR-PRA-08)
                            (BR-PRA-08)           v
                            exit             [9] compute_verdict(findings) (pure — BR-PRA-06/13)
                                                  |
                                                  v
                                            [10] Render summary_markdown
                                                  |
                                                  v
                                            [11] Post/refresh results to GitHub:
                                                  - upsert summary comment (idempotent — BR-PRA-14)
                                                  - inline comments for located findings
                                                  - set commit status on head SHA
                                                  - APPROVE review iff verdict == APPROVE
                                                  (re-review comment only if verdict changed — BR-PRA-09)
```

## Functions (logical, technology-agnostic)

### Pure functions (no I/O — primary PBT targets)
- `classify_findings(raw_findings) -> list[Finding]`: normalize/validate model output into typed Findings; drop malformed entries.
- `compute_verdict(findings, error, oversized) -> Verdict`: implements BR-PRA-06 precedence. Pure and deterministic.
- `render_summary(review_result) -> markdown string`: deterministic formatting of findings grouped by severity.
- `parse_model_response(text) -> list[raw_finding]`: parse the model's JSON payload; raise a typed error if unparseable.
- `detect_language(path) -> string`: map file extension to language.

### I/O functions (side effects — mocked in tests)
- `fetch_diff(context) -> list[DiffFile]`: GitHub API.
- `invoke_bedrock(prompt) -> text`: Bedrock runtime API.
- `upsert_summary_comment(context, body)`: GitHub API (idempotent via marker).
- `post_inline_comments(context, findings)`: GitHub API.
- `set_status(context, verdict)`: GitHub commit status API.
- `submit_approval(context)`: GitHub PR review API.

## Testable Properties (PBT-01 — Property-Based Testing extension ENABLED/Full)

| Component | Property Category | Property |
|---|---|---|
| `compute_verdict` | Invariant | If any finding is High → verdict is always BLOCK, regardless of other findings' order/count (BR-PRA-03). |
| `compute_verdict` | Invariant | If findings list is empty and no error/oversize → verdict is always APPROVE (BR-PRA-04). |
| `compute_verdict` | Invariant | If `error` is set → verdict is always ERROR, regardless of findings (fail-closed, BR-PRA-08). |
| `compute_verdict` | Commutativity | Verdict is independent of the ORDER of findings in the list (only their severities matter). |
| `compute_verdict` | Idempotence | `compute_verdict(f) == compute_verdict(f)` for repeated calls (deterministic, BR-PRA-13). |
| `parse_model_response` / `render_summary` | Round-trip | For a valid ReviewResult, `parse(render_findings_json(findings))` yields findings equal to the originals (structured serialize→deserialize). |
| `classify_findings` | Invariant | Every output Finding has a valid Severity and category; malformed inputs are dropped, never crash. |
| `classify_findings` | Idempotence | `classify(classify(x)) == classify(x)` (normalization is idempotent, BR-PRA-14 support). |
| `render_summary` | Invariant | Output never contains the token/credentials placeholder values (SECURITY-03 guard). |

Components with **no PBT properties**: I/O functions (`fetch_diff`, `invoke_bedrock`, GitHub posting) — these are integration-tested with mocks, not property-tested (they are thin API adapters). Marked as "No PBT properties identified — thin I/O adapters."

## Data Flow Summary
- **Inputs**: GitHub PR event (untrusted), PR diff (untrusted), config (MAX_DIFF_BYTES, model id, region).
- **Transformations**: diff → bounded ReviewInput → prompt → model response → findings → verdict → markdown.
- **Outputs**: GitHub comments, commit status, optional approval review, structured logs (no secrets).
